    "result_text": "Only one test class runs (the others are support classes). The full build is green.\n\nDone. The change adds `capacityWarning` as a derived read field, keeping structural impact minimal:\n\n- **New `OwnerCapacityWarningPolicy`** \u2014 a small, self-contained `@Component` mirroring `OwnerBulkSignupPolicy`. Its one `capacityWarning(Owner)` method returns `true` when the owner's city holds 40\u201349 owners (`count >= 40 && count < 50`), so 50+ stays false and the existing hard rejection at 50 is untouched.\n- **One `@Mapping` line** in `OwnerMapper` wiring the field during owner\u2192DTO mapping.\n- **OpenAPI `capacityWarning` property** on the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the boolean.\n\nNo existing method's body was grown and no large class was touched \u2014 the behaviour lives in a new cohesive unit with near-zero surrounding complexity.",
